# Copy this file to `.env` in this same folder, then paste in ONE key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The app picks whichever key it finds — you do not need to tell it which
# provider to use. With no key at all, every screen still works and
# worksheets show clearly-labelled sample content.
#
# This file is for the SEO Worksheet Studio only. Never paste a key that
# belongs to the BLC Worksheets project here, and never copy this file
# there — separate projects, separate credentials.

# ── Question writing — pick ONE ────────────────────────────────────

# Groq — fastest and has a free tier. https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# Anthropic — https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# OpenAI — https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# WHICH ONE WINS when more than one key is filled in.
# "auto" picks the first key it finds, in this order:
#       GROQ  ->  ANTHROPIC  ->  OPENAI
# So if you paste an OpenAI key in while a Groq key is still above it,
# Groq keeps being used and nothing appears to change. Either blank the
# key you have finished with, or name the one you want here:
#       LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# Valid values: auto | groq | anthropic | openai
LLM_PROVIDER=auto


# ── Pictures ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Worksheet diagrams (number lines, arrays, ten-frames, bar models,
# counters) are DRAWN BY PYTHON from a structured spec. They need no key,
# cost nothing, and are always arithmetically correct. That is the
# default and it is the right choice for maths.
#
# An image model is only worth adding for decorative or photo-real
# artwork ("children playing in a park"). Setting OPENAI_API_KEY above
# also enables that path — no separate key is needed.
#
# gpt-image-1 needs a VERIFIED OpenAI organisation. If you get a 403
# mentioning verification, change this to: dall-e-3
OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1

# ── Canva (optional, not required — and there's a real catch) ──────
#
# ⚠️  READ THIS BEFORE SPENDING TIME ON CANVA SETUP  ⚠️
#
# Canva's Autofill API — the one that would place a picture into a
# branded template — REQUIRES A CANVA ENTERPRISE PLAN. This is stated
# directly in Canva's own documentation: "To use the Brand Template and
# Autofill APIs, your integration must act on behalf of a user that's a
# member of a Canva Enterprise organization." If your team's plan is
# Free / Pro / Teams, none of this will work no matter what you paste
# in below — check your plan first.
#
# It's also NOT a simple key you paste in and you're done. Canva uses
# OAuth (a real person logs in and clicks "Allow" once) rather than a
# static API key. The three values below identify your INTEGRATION —
# after they're set, open the app, go to the Setup tab, and click
# "Connect Canva" to complete the actual connection.
#
# Setup, in order:
#   1. Confirm your Canva plan is Enterprise.
#   2. Log into https://www.canva.com/developers/ yourself (needs MFA
#      enabled on your Canva account — this step cannot be done by
#      an assistant or automated on your behalf).
#   3. Create an integration, note the Client ID, click "Generate
#      secret" and save it immediately (Canva will not show it again).
#   4. Design a Brand Template in the Canva UI with an image field and
#      any text fields you want autofilled, then copy its ID from the
#      published template's URL.
#   5. Paste all three values below, restart the app, then click
#      "Connect Canva" in the Setup tab.
CANVA_CLIENT_ID=
CANVA_CLIENT_SECRET=
CANVA_BRAND_TEMPLATE_ID=

# Where Canva sends the browser back to after approval. For local
# development, the default below is fine (Canva explicitly allows
# 127.0.0.1/localhost for dev). Must match EXACTLY what's registered in
# the integration's settings in the Canva Developer Portal. Change this
# — and the registered value — if the app runs anywhere other than your
# own machine on port 8020.
CANVA_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:8020/api/canva/callback

# Encrypts the Canva connection's tokens at rest in the database (this is
# a live, revocable connection, not a static key, so it's stored in the
# database rather than here). Generate one with:
#   python3 -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
# Safe to leave blank for a single local run — a key is derived
# automatically — but set this explicitly for anything shared or
# redeployed, or a restart can make stored tokens unreadable.
APP_SECRET_KEY=


# ── Shared Drive folder (team output, not a per-user key) ──────────
#
# This is where "Send to Drive" (on the Approved tab) uploads finished
# worksheets — organised into a subfolder per source category, so if
# several teammates each run their own independent copy of this tool and
# work on different K5 categories, their approved PDFs land in the same
# place without colliding. This is separate from, and unrelated to, any
# AI provider above.
#
# Setup (done ONCE by whoever owns the shared folder):
#   1. console.cloud.google.com -> create/select a project
#   2. Enable the "Google Drive API" for that project
#   3. Create a Service Account -> create a JSON key -> download it
#   4. Save the downloaded file as service_account.json in this same
#      folder (seo_math_worksheets/) — it's already gitignored
#   5. Open that JSON file, copy the "client_email" value
#   6. In Google Drive, right-click the shared folder -> Share -> paste
#      that email in -> give it Editor access
#   7. Copy the folder's ID from its URL (the part after /folders/)
#      into GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID below
#
# Full walkthrough with screenshoted steps: see the "Shared Drive folder"
# section in the top-level README.

# Only needed if service_account.json isn't sitting in this same folder.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_FILE=

GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=
